# Easy Quran Classes — root .env template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values there. `.env` is
# gitignored and blocked from Claude's Read/Edit tools and from common
# Bash/PowerShell read commands (see .claude/settings.json and
# .claude/hooks/guard-bash.mjs). Never paste real values into chat, commits,
# logs, or this example file.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE ACTUALLY IS: reference metadata for CPANEL-WORKFLOW.md.
# Nothing in this repo's code, scripts, or CI reads this file — grep it and
# see for yourself. It exists so the production/cPanel facts you need
# during a release are written down in one place, not so any tooling can
# consume them. If a key here stops being useful reference information,
# delete it; do not keep it "just in case a script starts using it".
#
# This hosting account has no Shell/SSH/Terminal access (confirmed) — do not
# add SSH/key variables here. cPanel deployment is manual, via File Manager
# and phpMyAdmin; see CPANEL-WORKFLOW.md. Nothing here is required until
# release/deployment work actually begins.

# --- Production site (reference only — read by nothing) -------------------
EQC_PROD_DOMAIN=https://easyquranclasses.com

# Staging site (if/when provisioned)
EQC_STAGING_DOMAIN=

# --- cPanel (reference only — read by nothing) -----------------------------
# The cPanel *password* does NOT belong here or anywhere in this file. Log
# into cPanel by hand (CLAUDE.md "cPanel / Production Boundary" — Claude
# does not automate cPanel login). This is just the URL/username so you
# don't have to hunt for them during a release.
EQC_CPANEL_URL=
EQC_CPANEL_USER=

# --- WordPress (reference only — read by nothing) --------------------------
EQC_WP_PATH=
EQC_WP_ADMIN_URL=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real secrets do NOT go in this file — not here, not in a personal section
# below. This file's protections (gitignore, the Read/Bash tool guards
# above) stop an agent from reading it back out through those tools; they do
# nothing for the file sitting in plaintext on disk, in an editor's recent-
# files list, or in whatever backs up this machine.
#
# Where real credentials actually belong:
#   - FTPS deploy password (used by .github/workflows/deploy.yml)
#       -> GitHub repo Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions
#          (FTP_SERVER, FTP_USERNAME, FTP_PASSWORD) — already set up this way.
#   - cPanel login password
#       -> a password manager. Not this file, not local/.env, not Git.
#   - SSH/PGP/deploy private keys, .pub files
#       -> this hosting account has no SSH (see CLAUDE.md) — there should be
#          no legitimate key material for this project at all. If you have
#          one for something else, it belongs in your OS keychain / SSH
#          agent, never a repo-adjacent file.
#   - Local WordPress admin password, Novamira Application Password
#       -> local/.env (a *different*, separate file — see local/.env.example
#          and README-SETUP.md §2.1). Those are local-dev-only values, never
#          production credentials, and local/.env has its own gitignore
#          entry and its own Read/Bash guard coverage.
#
# If you're reorganizing an existing .env that has drifted from this
# template: diff it against this file, move anything under the categories
# above out to its real home, and delete it from here once moved.
